    "title": "A Grip on Sports: The one thing we can count on in college athletics these days? The NCAA will always be on the wrong side of whatever issue pops up. - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Vince Grippi vincegrippi55@yahoo.com ,\n1 days ago A GRIP ON SPORTS • When we were a wee one, games at Dodger Stadium were circus-like. An organ played. There were a couple bigger-than-an-elephant players. And a barker, who used to scream “you can’t tell the players without a scorecard” as you walked through the gates. We think of that guy every time we read another story about NCAA eligibility litigation. Read full article",
